This is my third ascension (first was wizard, second was valkyrie).
The rogue was overall way  easier to ascend than the other two.

I started out with 10 orcish daggers, which isn't great, but it isn't
that bad either.  Starting  with daggers makes the Gnomish mines easier
than with other characters, because you already have  a means to get
rid of monsters that you really shouldn't melee.  The rogue also
doesn't need MP  to do ranged damage (i.e. wizard), and doesn't have to
worry about losing missile weapons to do  damage (i.e. ranger).  I
think the hardest part of the game is surviving the trip to the bottom
of the Gnomish Mines and back, so I really like the rogue class.

My new general strategy is to do the Gnomish Mines first, and to let
the pet kill things so that  I'm around character level 7-8 when I
reach the bottom of the mines.  Doing sokoban first puts  you at danger
of being too high an experience level before reaching the bottom of the
mines. In  the mines I collected the hard stones, the luck stone, the
normal daggers, the crossbow bolts,  the darts, whatever wands are
immediatly identifable, and a couple scrolls (the ones the showed  up
way more often than others, in hopes that one is an identify scroll).
Everything else gets  left behind.  I had to dump the pick axe on the
bottom level of the mines, so that I could  collect these items without
getting burdened.  I also had to dump the orcish daggers along the  way
too, because I didn't have enough strength to carry the orcish daggers
and the regular  daggers.  I also dumped my short sword for weight
reasons, and also because I never used it.

I also dump the pet at the bottom of the mines since I don't need it
anymore.  At this point I  already used the pet to find a set of
non-cursed armor, which put me at AC -3.  And I don't need  to keep my
level low anymore, since I already did the bottom of the mines.  I
think I actually  dumped the pet 1-2 levels away from the bottom of the
mines because it hit a level teleport trap  and I really didn't feel
like looking for it since I didn't have telepathy.

I dumped most my inventory off at minetown (to free up weight), and did
sokoban so I could have  enough food to allow me to sacrifice at
minetown until I max my luck out.  The max luck is  important for 2
reasons.  First reason is I think it lowers the chances of losing a
missle  weapon, and second reason is it helps find traps.  Since I
don't have magic resistance, I want  to lessen my chances of accidently
stepping in a polymorph trap.

Here's where things fell apart.  I killed the Minetown priest (he was a
different alignment),  and got about 6 altar conversion failures in a
row. Also, when I attacked the priest, some guard  blew his whistle, so
I had to kill all the remaining guards.  I had also killed one of the
shopkeepers around this time, as I was considering sacrificing him to
make a guaranteed altar  conversion, but I ended up not sacrificing
him.  I ended up converting the altar finally.  So  now I have a bunch
of ghosts roaming the town.  Also, for some reason, praying at the
altar  wasn't giving me stuff.  Like I'd just get a bunch of "is
well-pleased" messages.  I did end up  with 3 artifact sacrifice gifts
very quickly (Stormbringer, Frostband, and some useless  artifact).
After about 10 minutes of my luck not increasing (best praying reward I
got was a  couple of golden glows), I gave up with the altar thing.

The RNG also didn't provide enough crossbow bolts for the crossbow to
be a usable weapon.  Even  though I blessed the bolts and the crossbow,
my luck was so low that the bolts were getting lost  too quickly.  I
have a lot of darts due to dart traps.  I blessed the darts and
poisoned them.   It appears that even though my luck isn't maxed, that
the darts have a much lower chance of  disappearing than the crossbow
bolts.

After I found Medusa's level, I dumped most my inventory near the fort
level, and did my mass  sweeping of the dungeon so far.

Mass sweeping means I go through every level I've been to, and collect
all the magical items,  potions, scrolls, rings, wands, and darts that
I missed along the way.  I also picked up  Frostbrand and some bear
traps.  And I quaffed the fountains to get my stats maxed out.  I also
read a couple books since my int was high enough to read them finally.

I hit XL14 during the Fort, so I left to do the quest.  I gathered some
booze potions (the  bottom of the mines was the wine cellar version),
and some teleportation scrolls (which were  identified for me by some
monster reading it), and did the quest.  The quest wouldn't be so bad
if it wasn't for the part where you can get literally stuck on the
bottom level of the quest if  you aren't careful.  I kept falling into
the wrong part of the bottom level (the part without  stairs and
without the quest nemesis), and accidently used up all my booze
potions.  I finally  fell into the correct part of the bottom level.
So I killed the nemesis, looted his body, and  noticed that I'm out of
booze potions.  I have plenty of teleportation scrolls, but I'm still
at  least 15,000 turns away from any spells getting forgotten.

So I used a very careful balance of my food, the monsters I created by
stepping into a magic  trap, and praying... until my spells finally got
forgotten.  Then I casted a forgotten spell,  and level-teleported out
of that level.

After the quest, Fort, and castle, I did my polymorph run.  I moved
everything worth  polymorphing into the Fort, and zapped piles of
stuff.  I got a book of identify, so I skilled  up divination.  Up to
this point I used the shop ID thing twice.  Once to figure out which
scroll is identify, and once to find a spellbook I could read in case I
needed a way to confuse  myself later.  The polymorph run wasn't very
exciting.  It did give me a shirt and long sword  though (which didn't
exist outside of the polymorphing).  So I wished for whatever I didn't
get  by polymorphing (I had to wish for a book of magic mapping).  And
here comes the second hardest  part of the game.  The part where you
have 849238054235 items, and you have to decide which ones  to bring
with you to the rest of the game.  I also finally got my AC below -5.

I used the fort money to donate at the valley of the dead priest (which
was the only time I ever donated money)

Nothing exciting happened until the Ascension run.  I used my mass
amounts of digging wands to  quickly run all the way up to the Plane of
Air.  I also used used my leftover teleportation  scrolls, and the ^T
teleport spell to speed up the ascension run.

On the Astral plane I blasted everything with either a wand of death,
or a wand of  teleportation.   I made my way over to the altar on the
right (the Death rider was blocking the  other sides, and you can't hit
him with death/teleportation).  It was a lawful altar.  So I put  on
the helm of opposite alignment, and offered the amulet.

